    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278-a4">

                <pb facs="0667" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg571"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4, in No. 179.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr.
                            Ethéart.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United Stattes</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 11,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Your dispatch dated on the 10th
                    instant, in which you notify me of the resolution which your government has
                    taken with regard to vessels (<hi rendition="#italic">les embarcations</hi>)
                    sent from the two cities of St. Marc and Gonaives to this port bearing packages,
                    has been received.</p>
                <p>Reserving all rights that appertain to my government and its consular officers
                    residing in this republic, and especially for the time being, with sentiments of
                    highest consideration, I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
